silm:instances_papers_07_the_canonical_question_chapters_05_free_construction_and_quotient_sections_01_free_generation_concrete_anchor_1#mittenscanonicalquestion silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensCanonicalQuestion is the canonical question of paper 07 posed of the running Mittens fixture: `what answers does this admit?' read as Hom_O(Q_07, -). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Q_{07}', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
